                  {
                      "parameters":  {
                                         "content":  "## Template Notes\n\nThis workflow is designed for consent-based abandoned checkout recovery by SMS.\n\nBefore publishing or using in production:\n\n- Replace placeholder Shopify store URL values.\n- Configure HTTP Header Auth for Shopify instead of hardcoding API keys.\n- Configure RCSZilla, OpenAI, and Google Sheets credentials in n8n.\n- Confirm your SMS consent and opt-out process matches the laws that apply to your store and customers.\n- Test with one internal checkout before activating a production schedule.",
                                         "height":  320,
                                         "width":  1300,
                                         "color":  4
                                     },
                      "id":  "ef86a495-60f4-49c0-a5ca-bbc4b36724b8",
                      "name":  "Sticky Note9",
                      "type":  "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
                      "position":  [
                                       368,
                                       240
                                   ],
                      "typeVersion":  1
                  },
                  {
                      "parameters":  {
                                         "content":  "## Description\n\nRecover abandoned Shopify checkouts with AI-written SMS messages sent through RCSZilla.\n\nThe workflow fetches abandoned Shopify checkouts, waits one hour, checks whether the shopper is still abandoned, validates phone/SMS consent data, generates a short recovery SMS, queues it with RCSZilla, and logs the result to Google Sheets.\n\n## Setup Guide\n\n1. Install the RCSZilla community node package: n8n-nodes-rcszilla.\n2. Create an RCSZilla API credential in n8n.\n3. Create an OpenAI credential for the SMS writer model.\n4. Create an HTTP Header Auth credential for Shopify with header name X-Shopify-Access-Token and your Admin API access token as the value.\n5. Replace your-store.myshopify.com in both Shopify HTTP Request nodes.\n6. Configure the Google Sheets node with your own spreadsheet and these columns: customer, phone, checkout_url, sms_message, rcszilla_response.\n7. Run the workflow manually with a test abandoned checkout, then replace the Manual Trigger with a Schedule Trigger for production.\n\n## Compliance Notes\n\nOnly send SMS to customers who have opted in to SMS marketing. Keep the STOP opt-out text in the generated message. Do not use this workflow for unsolicited messages.",
                                         "height":  2238,
                                         "width":  1289,
                                         "color":  4
                                     },
                      "id":  "0f722fcc-e05a-4b9d-9250-487a049779eb",
